; <rdar://problem/10368487> Contact problems if you have "siri" as user data
leading noise
    ; TODO need a better way to match start constraints
    {hi|hey|hello|yo|g{'}day|good day|howdy|hola} {please|there} Siri {(can|will) you} {please} [conf=vh][exists;constraint=start;strict=true]
    ; The following variations of the above have been as part of the Pre DC Rules effort
    {hi|hey|hello|yo|g{'}day|good day|howdy|hola} {Siri} {(could|will|would) you|(i'd|i would) like you {to}} please {Siri} [conf=vh][exists;constraint=start;strict=true]
    {hi|hey|hello|yo|g{'}day|good day|howdy|hola} {Siri} ((could|will|would) you|(i'd|i would) like you {to}) {please} {Siri} [conf=vh][exists;constraint=start;strict=true]

    {hi|hey|hello|yo|g{'}day|good day|howdy|hola}
    and
    but
    {no} i said
    (yes|yeah|yep|yup|sure)[notExists;constraint=start][notExists;node=sms;constraint=strictPrompt]
    oh
    (yes|yeah|yep|yup|sure) but
    so
    excuse me


;<rdar://problem/10287714> "I want a reminder please", "please" is used as the reminder topic
trailing noise [conf=vh]
    please {siri} [exists;constraint=end;strict=true]

leading or trailing noise
    please [conf=vh]
    Siri [conf=vh] [notExists="for,about,concerning,with,by,from,to,in,of";constraint=adjBefore]
    (ok|okay) [exists;constraint=start][notExists;constraint=end]
    thank{s}
    thank you
    now

